  "question": {
    "text": "<p>In figure (A), mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>m</mi></math>&nbsp;is fixed on mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math>&nbsp;which is attached to two springs of spring constant <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>k</mi></math>. In figure (B), mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math>&nbsp;is attached to two spring of spring constant <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>k</mi></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>k</mi></math>. If mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math>&nbsp;in (A) and (B) are displaced by distance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>&nbsp;horizontally and then released, then time period <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> corresponding to (A) and (B) respectively follow the relation.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/45749699-b2e8-4db1-b0b1-eda289f4dbe5-image.png\" style=\"width: 380px; height: 132px;\" /></p>",
    "image": null
  },
